AB  - The proceedings contain 218 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Computer-Aided Architectural Design Research in Asia. The topics include: LLM-Driven Architectural Geometry Generation: From Prompt to Parametric Model; Carbon-Conscious Design Agents: A Multi-Agent LLM Framework for Balancing Embodied Carbon and Cost in Early Building Design; visual Sentiment Cartography: Exploring Collective Urban Visual Experiences Through Machine Learning; Tacit to Explicit: LLM-Augmented Pattern Language for Representing Architectural Design Knowledge; encoding Transitions: Self-Supervised Learning of Architectural Thresholds with Masked Spatiotemporal Transformers; designing Cooler Cities with Tree Canopy Morphology Insights An interactive evaluation tool using interpretable machine learning; Interpreting User Responses as Emotional Evidence in Spatial Design Using EEG: A Pilot Study Toward Emotion-Informed Design Recommendation; Chain-of-Design: Sequencing Agentic AI Design Reasoning for Architecture in 3D; archGraph: Knowledge Graph-Driven Intelligence for Architectural History: A Case Study on Palladio's Architecture; Modular Neural Cellular Automata (m-NCA): A Physics-Informed Framework for Real-Time Dynamic Simulation in Architectural Design; semantic Drift in Architectural Research: A Diachronic Analysis Using Word Embedding; architectural Prompts as Design Intent: An Experimental Study of Information Transmission in Text-to-Image Generation; sensing Street Rhythm: A Natural Language Processing-Based Approach: Mapping Human Perception by Understanding Deep Semantic Features in Street View Images; latent Maps for Architectural Reasoning: Multi-Modal Precedent Retrieval as Real-Time Context for Design; Developing an Agentic AI Framework with MCP for Knowledge Continuity in AEC Industry; Human-in-the-Loop Selection for AI-Assisted Point Cloud Reconstruction: Evaluating Designer Agency with Ground Truth; a Hierarchical N-ary Relation Extraction Method for St