AB  - The present article focuses on detailing the characteristics of Afanasyev, an architectural framework for the construction of story generation systems through replaceable services. The basic idea behind this approach is the development of a collaborative environment for generating stories. This entails the inclusion of a common representation model to allow the interoperation between different story generation systems as a base for a collaborative environment to run an enhanced process of literary creation. In addition to this objective, this model aims at the development of a story representation formalism for creating a common knowledge base that can be fed in the future with the outcomes of new storytelling systems, without the need to adapt it to every system-specific representation model. © Proceedings of AISB Annual Convention 2018. All rights reserved.
