AB  - A methodology for validation is provided for the architecture of Knowledge based Engineering (KBE) applications. A standard approach to validation is introduced, followed by the Synergistic Validation Methodology (SVM), which addresses four key aspects of KBE system validation: a) software architecture, b) product design process, c) artificial intelligence, and d) knowledge acquisition. The synergistic methodology is introduced as a comprehensive approach to validation of Knowledge-based engineering systems. This SVM approach is shown to be divided into four target divisions addressing multiple areas each, which correspond to well-defined methodologies in terms of general standards, techniques, and methods utilized. The five-tier pre-validation and post-validation process is intended to verify and validate reconfigurable, modular, and scalable KBE systems.
