AB  - The proceedings contain 15 papers from the Recent Trends in Algebraic Development Techniques - 17th International Workshop, WADT 2004. The topics discussed include: behavior-preserving refinement relations between dynamic software architectures; cryptomorphisms at work; towards a formal specification of an electronic payment system in CSP-CASL; algebraic semantics of design abstractions for context-awareness; ontologies for the semantic web in CASL; behavioural semantics of algebraic specifications in arbitrary logical systems; a simple refinement language for CASL; a distributed and mobile component system based on the ambient calculus; and type class polymorphism in an institutional framework.
